# What `docker build` sends to the daemon. Everything is excluded, then the four files
# and the one directory the Dockerfile copies are put back: written the other way round,
# a list of exclusions, it would have to grow with every directory added to the
# repository, and whatever it forgot would ship. Left out this way: the tests, the
# evaluations, the benchmarks, the documentation site with its node_modules, the Claude
# Desktop extension, the Claude Code plugin, the virtual environment, the caches, and
# the git history, which holds every version of all of them.
*
!LICENSE
!README.md
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!avenir_mcp

# Compiled bytecode of a local run, which came back with avenir_mcp: the image compiles
# its own, for the Python it ships.
avenir_mcp/**/__pycache__
